{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>But if you shall surely keep… to love.</b> That your engagement in the Torah be for the sake of recognizing the loving kindness of the Most High El — for from this, love follows." "<b>And to walk in all His ways.</b> To conduct yourself in those ways by which He governs His world — namely, righteousness and justice." "<b>And to cleave to Him.</b> That all your deeds be directed toward doing His will, as it says: בְּכָל דְּרָכֶיךָ דָעֵהוּ (Proverbs 3:6)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:14.193349645Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}